From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikael Rousson <85865+mmmikael@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 08:35:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/15] foyelle: MCP Apps surfaces in the gateway

Hermes dropped tool _meta, so ui:// resources (SEP-1865) never reached a
client. tools/mcp_surfaces.py records which registered MCP tools declare
_meta.ui.resourceUri, reads the HTML resource over the live session and
converts tool results to the CallToolResult shape an MCP App expects.

The gateway gains a surface.open event, emitted after such a tool
completes, and four RPCs on the long-handler pool: surface.list,
surface.open_resource, surface.read_resource and surface.call_tool. A
surface's own tool call is dispatched through handle_function_call with
the session's approval context bound, so plugins (Foyelle's policy
engine and audit log) and the approval gate treat it like a model call;
mcp_surfaces.current_origin() tells them it came from a surface.

Contracts are declared in tui_gateway/contracts/surfaces.py and the
generated TypeScript contract is regenerated.

Signed-off-by: Mikael Rousson <85865+mmmikael@users.noreply.github.com>
